==English==
[[Image:Illu testis surface.jpg|thumb|1: Epididymis<BR>2: Head of epididymis<BR>3: Lobules of epididymis<BR>4: Body of epididymis<BR>5: Tail of epididymis<BR>6: Duct of epididymis<BR>7: Deferent duct (ductus deferens or [[vas deferens]])]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ἐπιδιδυμίς}}, from {{m|grc|ἐπί||upon, over}} + {{m|grc|δίδυμος||testicle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɛpiˈdɪdɪmɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|epididymides}}

# {{label|en|anatomy}} A narrow, tightly-coiled tube connecting the [[efferent duct]]s from the rear of each [[testicle]] to its [[vas deferens]], where [[sperm]] are stored during maturation.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|paratesticle}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|epididymal}}
* {{l|en|epididymitis}}

